WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.390
- I'm starting to get nauseous

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.010
and I'm starting to feel lost.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:04.300
And I forget what time we got here

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.970
- Let's just set up camp here.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.570
(lively rag time music playing)

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:14.900
- I know that it is Swedish.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.610
- I imagine it's gotta be pretty big.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:17.900
- If there's one thing I was raised to do,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.480
it's to hunt a good deal.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.150
So if the deals are
good, I'm gonna love it.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.540
- It's supposed to be a sort of a circus,

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.470
and I really enjoy shopping
and circuses, so...

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.110
(lively rag time music playing)

00:00:30.152 --> 00:00:31.580
- It looks like a 90's roller coaster.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.790
(lively rag time music playing)

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.402
- There's a challenge?

00:00:34.402 --> 00:00:35.900
Find the cheapest desk

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.370
- The best couch.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.020
- And pasta and everything to make pasta.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.510
- Ooh, look at their
tasteful use of crates.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.760
- This is what happens when Pac-Man dies.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:47.720
You skin him and you make him into these.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.150
- Help, I'm trapped in an IKEA shower.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.133
- This chair can withstand
even the slowest (beeping).

00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:59.810
- So, we've lost Katie
in the depths of IKEA.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:00.932
- She could be anywhere.

00:01:00.932 --> 00:01:03.120
- We're gonna have to
backtrack to find her.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.730
- Bed number one, bed number
two, bed number three.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.070
Let's chase some birds!

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.120
- There she is.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.620
- Best one, found the best mattress.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:12.833
Found it.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:15.790
- You think, like, we can haggle?

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:17.420
- We haven't seen light in hours.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.040
We don't know how long it's been.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.830
I just wanna, like, spend money now.

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:23.610
(lively rag time music playing)

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.420
- When I started I was very
excited, cuz I love shopping.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.002
- We were like little ants,

00:01:29.002 --> 00:01:31.140
finding our way through the ant tunnel,

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.010
- And then immediately
when we got upstairs,

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:34.310
I found salad spinners.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.263
This is step one on my pasta journey.

00:01:36.263 --> 00:01:38.810
Because I always use my
salad spinner as my strainer.

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.680
- Things were laid out very cute,

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:41.940
but then you get a couple rooms deep

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.770
and you realize that you're
just in this apartment

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.180
that goes on forever.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.780
- And then eventually we found the map.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:47.780
We realized when we got to this map,

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:49.200
this place was (beeping) huge.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.420
- You keep going along a path,

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.580
but it's not really
clear where it's going.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.040
And like the deeper you
go, the creepier it got

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.760
with, like, people's clothes being there.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.412
I can't take any of it off.

00:02:01.082 --> 00:02:02.750
Joke's on you, I'm takin' these.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:05.300
- There were probably
more comfortable couches

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.420
than the one I picked,

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.050
but I liked how mine looked.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.500
This is the couch I picked, the URKSA.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.810
Cuz I love the orange color of it

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.890
and the name reminds me of
Steve Urkle's girlfriend.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:17.560
- The next one was the cheapest desk,

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:21.690
which I think I found because
I found a laptop table.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:25.250
40 dollars, 40 dollars is
the cheapest desk easily.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.490
- We finally reached
the middle of the store,

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:28.710
we were exhausted, we thought

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:29.940
this must be the end of the store.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:31.830
It was actually only the half way point.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.360
But this was where they
had the famous IKEA food.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.080
Which, to their credit,
that food is really cheap.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:43.050
- And so then, we had to
make it out through another

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.290
half of the store, which then became

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:48.940
tiny little plates, and
candles, and lamps, and stuff.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.260
- Wait, now grab a cart.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.120
- I won't have to sleep
on that couch anymore.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.350
- Why are we grabbing a cart?

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.350
- Wait, are we only now at
the part where you buy stuff?

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.380
- That was initially confusing,

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.690
because I started to look
for pasta stuff right away,

00:02:58.690 --> 00:02:59.850
and it was sort of scattered

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.520
throughout the different kitchens.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:02.770
There's no bowls.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.150
Where do we...

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.182
What do we have?

00:03:05.182 --> 00:03:07.970
- We're gonna have to turn
into a new location for bowls.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.010
- All of a sudden, we go
down to this marketplace,

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.790
and now there it all is.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:15.870
Pasta, (clapping) four bowls,

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.000
some forks, strainer, pot.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.250
Nailed it!

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.920
The marketplace was a weird purgatory.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.750
- But this is the area
where I started getting

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.290
pretty impressed with the prices.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.202
- You got three bucks?

00:03:26.202 --> 00:03:27.890
I got a lamp for you.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:29.910
And so after you make it
through all the store parts,

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.420
then you go to the warehouse.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:32.800
- It was like a Home Depot

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.500
but there was nobody there to help you.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.990
- Do we have to build them?

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:37.970
And set up a display for
whole new set of customers?

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:38.800
- Oh wait, wait, wait.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.480
Do we get to use the forklift?

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:41.270
- Do we work here now?

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:42.230
They had these computers

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.690
where you look up a numbering system

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.110
to find the thing that you're looking for.

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:47.110
EKTORP, EKTORP. I found it.

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:49.480
The numbering system has
nothing to do with the order

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.160
that they're actually
placed in along the walls.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.030
So, then I just had to look for the name,

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:54.860
and Katie made fun of me

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.780
for even trying to use the number system.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:57.280
- What can I say?

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.610
I went in, looked for my couch, found it.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:00.260
I won!

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.940
- I would say IKEA actually
exceeded my expectations

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:09.950
because I didn't think it would be so big.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:13.220
- The idea of going back now, is terrible.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:14.170
I don't wanna go back.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.230
But those prices were so low.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:19.080
- I bought a memory foam
pillow for 13 bucks.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.720
- I would probably go back.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.470
- It was an emotional roller coaster.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.310
I think people say, like, if you want

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:28.000
a relationship to last,
you should travel together.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.990
But I think what they mean to say is,

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:31.290
if you want a relationship to last

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.580
you should travel to IKEA together.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.842
- [Voiceover] Restrooms may
be located near the restroom,

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:38.750
but there's toilets right here.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.850
- So, Danion what are you
doing to the bathroom?

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.812
- What does anyone do in the bathroom?

00:04:43.812 --> 00:04:45.582
It's private business.

